{"declarations":[{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span>\n<span class=\"decl_name\"><a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Lean/Meta/Sym/Canon.html#Lean.Meta.Sym.canon\"><span class=\"name\">Lean</span>.<span class=\"name\">Meta</span>.<span class=\"name\">Sym</span>.<span class=\"name\">canon</span></a></span><span class=\"decl_args\">\n<span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">e</span> : <a href=\"./Lean/Expr.html#Lean.Expr\">Expr</a>)</span></span>\n<span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Lean/Meta/Sym/SymM.html#Lean.Meta.Sym.SymM\">SymM</a> <a href=\"./Lean/Expr.html#Lean.Expr\">Expr</a></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Canonicalize `e` by normalizing types, instances, and support arguments.\nApplies targeted reductions (projection, match/ite/cond, Nat arithmetic) in all positions;\neta reduction is applied only inside types. Instances are re-synthesized.\nRuns at reducible transparency.\n","docLink":"./Lean/Meta/Sym/Canon.html#Lean.Meta.Sym.canon","kind":"def","line":576,"name":"Lean.Meta.Sym.canon","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/11acb17ec6b07a8f9e9173e6845197929540936b/src/Lean/Meta/Sym/Canon.lean#L576-L583"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span>\n<span class=\"decl_name\"><a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Lean/Meta/Sym/Canon.html#Lean.Meta.Sym.Canon.isSupport\"><span class=\"name\">Lean</span>.<span class=\"name\">Meta</span>.<span class=\"name\">Sym</span>.<span class=\"name\">Canon</span>.<span class=\"name\">isSupport</span></a></span><span class=\"decl_args\">\n<span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">pinfos</span> : <span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Array\">Array</a> <a href=\"./Lean/Meta/Basic.html#Lean.Meta.ParamInfo\">ParamInfo</a></span>)</span></span>\n<span class=\"decl_args\">\n<span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">i</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Nat\">Nat</a>)</span></span>\n<span class=\"decl_args\">\n<span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">arg</span> : <a href=\"./Lean/Expr.html#Lean.Expr\">Expr</a>)</span></span>\n<span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Lean/Meta/Basic.html#Lean.Meta.MetaM\">MetaM</a> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Bool\">Bool</a></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Returns `true` if `shouldCanon pinfos i arg` is not `.visit`.\nThis is a helper function used to implement mbtc.\n","docLink":"./Lean/Meta/Sym/Canon.html#Lean.Meta.Sym.Canon.isSupport","kind":"def","line":566,"name":"Lean.Meta.Sym.Canon.isSupport","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/11acb17ec6b07a8f9e9173e6845197929540936b/src/Lean/Meta/Sym/Canon.lean#L566-L572"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span>\n<span class=\"decl_name\"><a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Lean/Meta/Sym/Canon.html#Lean.Meta.Sym.Canon.normNumLit?\"><span class=\"name\">Lean</span>.<span class=\"name\">Meta</span>.<span class=\"name\">Sym</span>.<span class=\"name\">Canon</span>.<span class=\"name\">normNumLit?</span></a></span><span class=\"decl_args\">\n<span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">e</span> : <a href=\"./Lean/Expr.html#Lean.Expr\">Expr</a>)</span></span>\n<span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Lean/Meta/Basic.html#Lean.Meta.MetaM\">MetaM</a> <span class=\"fn\">(<a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Option\">Option</a> <a href=\"./Lean/Expr.html#Lean.Expr\">Expr</a>)</span></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Normalizes numeric literals of wrapping types during canonicalization. Two kinds of\nnon-canonical spellings are handled:\n- `BitVec.ofNat`/`BitVec.ofNatLT`/`Fin.ofNat` applications with literal arguments (e.g.,\n  `1#2`, `Fin.ofNat 3 2`) are converted into the `OfNat.ofNat` representation.\n- `OfNat.ofNat` literals of `Fin` and the fixed-width types (see `getLitValueModulus?`) whose numeral\n  is out of range (e.g., `(300 : UInt8)`) are reduced modulo the type's cardinality.\n\nDifferent representations of the same literal may reach the canonicalizer (e.g., the proposition\nof a `dite` `Decidable` instance keeps the spelling used in the source), and `grind`\nassumes distinct interpreted nodes denote distinct values (see `valueInconsistency` at\n`Grind.addEqStep`), so all representations of the same literal must canonicalize to the same\nterm. The result is definitionally equal to the input.\n","docLink":"./Lean/Meta/Sym/Canon.html#Lean.Meta.Sym.Canon.normNumLit?","kind":"def","line":141,"name":"Lean.Meta.Sym.Canon.normNumLit?","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/11acb17ec6b07a8f9e9173e6845197929540936b/src/Lean/Meta/Sym/Canon.lean#L141-L173"}}],"imports":["Init.Grind.Util","Lean.Meta.AppBuilder","Lean.Meta.IntInstTesters","Lean.Meta.LitValues","Lean.Meta.NatInstTesters","Lean.Meta.Sym.Arith.EvalNum","Lean.Meta.Sym.Eta","Lean.Meta.Sym.ExprPtr","Lean.Meta.Sym.SymM","Lean.Meta.Sym.SynthInstance","Lean.Meta.SynthInstance","Lean.Meta.WHNF"],"instances":[],"name":"Lean.Meta.Sym.Canon"}